{"schemaVersion":"1.0.0","kind":"eigenquestions-fine-index","destinations":[{"id":"source-question:a7663a5b5a4c8afd9b9e96161463b9f1e47306472c5d2b1102b0a67cb46d7010","title":"Can the maximal-supergravity multiplet be isolated from string theory while gravitational interactions remain at finite strength? The question requires examining additional nonperturbative states as well as perturbative string excitations.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0000"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:a727b64eab87223cc4d4ac4151fdddb01bfa16692c58e7b096151cda1be54fdf","title":"Can the charge-return argument survive if massive species decay, provided their lifetimes exceed the relevant black-hole evaporation time?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0001"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:a7425bf08bc51b478f636dfda6ad9c5aeaf1705325509bbd76df72abe6da736e","title":"Do complex Euclidean wormholes exist in compactified supergravity, and can string theory include their saddle-point contributions? The paper distinguishes the classical existence problem from the compatibility of a complex integration contour with discrete gauge symmetry.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0002"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:a7450cd3203ce6b46f6e7c6a548cacadf3d949aad21d87dcac5ebf97fc87e814","title":"Do supersymmetric AdS4 domain walls possess attractor equations fixing horizon scalars independently of suitable asymptotic data?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0002"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:a761021cd8a2aed1fcb8fd112301b3a533527f84a1e7c74878467f1ca0046a14","title":"Can Mellin amplitudes provide a useful definition of AdS scattering amplitudes, and can their large-variable asymptotics recover the bulk flat-space S-matrix?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0010"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:a7951b1a1bf3c3b2a19ae12c1a96332fa73b002b005e1cf099296e057dfa6a10","title":"Can kinetic mixing among N sub-Planckian axions produce a collective displacement exceeding their Pythagorean range, and under what conditions can inflation follow that enlarged direction?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0016"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:a74f6b932234857236f09f320de23e5654f9ca2458371340e25ba125ffb69e09","title":"Can the anti-D3 uplifting term be understood through spontaneously broken supersymmetry and a nilpotent goldstino multiplet, and why does an orientifolded anti-D3 produce this contribution while a D3 does not? The explicit calculation isolates the role of the fermionic Wess-Zumino term.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0017"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:a78f72ee47933d926710be6d0e61e986a92beefaef580a06be266f63461a3d04","title":"Can supergravity with one inflaton multiplet and one nilpotent multiplet describe inflation, a positive late-time vacuum energy and adjustable supersymmetry breaking, while avoiding additional Polonyi scalars and simplifying the fermionic super-Higgs sector?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0017"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:a76a941a3b8967bab4cc5afaff79ff7d8ef16a1a3489ecfcaa3ca637606ba0c0","title":"Does an exactly evaluated, nonlinearly anisotropic minisuperspace implementation of the no-boundary path integral yield a physically acceptable state with damped perturbations? The paper examines how initial momentum regularity and the complex lapse contour affect disputed enhancement of anisotropies.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0028"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:a743e3b068ed20bfc6952de40c1d8e423421f957cc92167bddd842e051730c0f","title":"The relevant quantity is a massless hypermultiplet charge in a specified six-dimensional gauge theory. Charge normalization must be tracked with anomaly data, and the non-Higgsable SU(3) spectator must be included when identifying the full gauge group.","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0032"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:a791a6e127c555447d1494cc8311c8776aa91aaf5c5053ae98f8a9cecf29d91d","title":"Which rational, family-dependent U(1)F charge assignments cancel all gauge and mixed gauge-gravity anomalies for SM fermions, optionally supplemented by up to three right-handed neutrinos, and how can these assignments be classified and enumerated?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0036"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:a7213e005778086953020c257c8c1837c29119e74e61917ab2ed5ebf1be86e63","title":"How do modulus and KK scales behave in a type IIA AdS flux family with a dilute-flux limit?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0046"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:a73f05de86b9bbd556c6838740af716b6069e20ee9380818ef33127c30345760","title":"Can an S3 scalar leptoquark explain the source-era neutral-current B anomalies while protecting proton stability and charged-lepton flavour, and can its extra gauge sector decouple without destabilizing scalar masses?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0056"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:a7598adbe03e2639ecc87aad679b23c115d94591604634847142e7291b64fb58","title":"Does consistency of the classical holographic dictionary force trapped surfaces behind event horizons, establishing this consequence of weak cosmic censorship without assuming the full initial-data conjecture?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0060"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:a