ance, matter-density and structure-growth signatures could reveal the interaction?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0103"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:a721fa4f6c9ecb5fd56259d8c57f59ef2cf8eb160550d5467215814bb10e0ce7","title":"Can known open-string models be understood as orbifolds of closed-string theories, with their boundaries, Chan–Paton multiplicities, and consistency conditions arising from world-sheet geometry and modular invariance?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0109"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:a7ab33080f7d99840254c9350b2c1dcb46803a74ea99a67d199a820eced44ca9","title":"Can time-dependent compactifications of classical String/M-theory supergravity produce accelerating four-dimensional cosmologies despite the SEC no-go theorem, and when is acceleration transient, unavoidable, or compatible with absence of a future event horizon?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0110"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-question:a741c99ea00d61ae2c87cd25f3e8656453f01bca5c2469aa09a660b7d35d8da9","title":"Can the horizon area and entropy of supersymmetric extremal black holes be obtained by extremizing the central charge over moduli, explaining their independence from asymptotic scalar values?","connectionCount":1,"detail":{"shardId":"destination-details-fine-0119"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"}],"relations":[{"id":"source-access:7e5ab25b57013b8ea07c7409","source":"q025-candidate-question:b2c54c1a873c70c5aa1f0159","target":"source-question:a7663a5b5a4c8afd9b9e96161463b9f1e47306472c5d2b1102b0a67cb46d7010","detail":{"shardId":"relation-details-0039","recordSha256":"47ea9263c7afcda3ba83775c87ab8b7eb29cf20d20ba5d48bd6290dac45ca9ed"},"indexTemplate":"source_question"},{"id":"source-access:0da41637fc96579f532046c2","source":"q025-candidate-question:e3c2b2b257c2287a7feef88c","target":"source-question:a727b6